/math] times)\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the product of the two fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(\\frac{3}{5})^{2} &= \\frac{3}{5} \\cdot \\frac{3}{5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3 \\cdot 3}{5 \\cdot 5} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{25}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)^2= \\dfrac{9}{25}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1065 8806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f0e87aeb-338c-5f8d-be18-59b85ed28aac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186148793 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488458 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186489301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488458 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488458 #edb/ref 1045 "Decimal and Fraction Operations Applied to Commercial Settings" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488458 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186489301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488458 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "8832ccc5-5062-53eb-9aa3-cff46feb853b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488613 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{16}{25}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488613 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488613 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47cde53f-47d7-5ae4-8572-e9ac9bf6754d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488751 #edb/ref 1080 "0.84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488751 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488751 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8d1c2dc7-edf8-570a-812f-d15c687b21fd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488776 #edb/ref 1080 "21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488776 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488776 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "988f552d-7fef-5802-8752-162edc8a6d1b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488831 #edb/ref 1080 "2.29" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488831 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186488831 #edb/ref 108