 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489172 #edb/ref 1084 #edb/ref 17592186489354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489172 #edb/ref 1085 "A construction company is building $5$ identical houses on a ${(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}$ square mile plot of land." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489172 #edb/ref 1086 #uuid "10b798da-88e8-599e-9a89-b5ff9c361f9a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489172 #edb/ref 1087 #edb/ref 17592186489302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489186 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489186 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166802" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489186 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489186 #edb/ref 1071 "The company used $104.7\\,\\text{ft}$ of piping to construct $5$ identical houses. Estimate the length of piping used for each home by rounding the total piping length to the nearest whole number.\n\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{ft}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489186 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1e21dfbe-7205-50ca-b839-4d1dcb287bbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489186 #edb/ref 1074 "To estimate the length of piping used for each of the $5$ houses, we need to find an approximation for $104.7÷5.$\n\nSo, we round the dividend to the nearest whole number:\n\n$$\n104.7\\to 105\n$$\n\nNow, we divide $105$ by $5$ as usual:\n\n$$\n105÷5=21\n$$\n\nTherefore, the construction of each house used approximately $21\\,\\text{ft}$ of pipes." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489188 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489188 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166798" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489188 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489188 #edb/ref 1071 "Building company policy states that each ton of cement mixture should contain at least $0.7$ tons of sand. What's the minimum amount of sand in $1.2$ tons of cement mixture? Express your answer as a decimal.\n\nThere will be a minimum of\n{{field-1}}\ntons of sand in $1.2$ tons of cement mixture." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489188 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "215d1b37-57d3-50ad-9730-b954c879d087" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489188 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine how much sand is in $1.2$ tons of the cement mixture, we have to multiply $1.2$ by $0.7.$\n\nWe proceed by multiplying the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers.\n\nNotice that the second number has a leading $0$, which we ignore during the multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.7\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in $1.2$ and there is $1$ decimal place in $0.7.$\nTherefore, their product will have $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n\nSo, we take our value of $84$ and add a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\n\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{84}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nHence, $1.2\\times 0.7=0.84.$\n\nWe conclude that there are $0.84$ tons of sand in $1.2$ tons of the cement mixture." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489228 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489228 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166799" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489228 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489228 #edb/ref 1071 "The building company combines $1.6$ tons of sand with $0.69$ tons of cement to make their cement mixture. What is the total weight of the mixture? Express your answer as a decimal.\n\nThe total weight of the mixture is\n{{field-1}}\ntons." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489228 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6535052d-d80b-57f3-9a80-25b64c4c2047" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489228 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the total weight of the mixture, we need to calculate the sum $1.6+0.69.$\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in $1.6$ and $2$ decimal places in $0.69.$\n\nTo add the numbers, they both need to have the same number of decimals. Hence, we rewrite the first number so that it has $2$ decimal places:\n\n$$\n1.6=1.60\n$$\n\nNext, we line up the decimal points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by adding the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total weight of the mixture is $2.29$ tons." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489236 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489236 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166797" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489236 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489236 #edb/ref 1071 "Expressed as a single fraction, the exact area of the plot of land is$\\,${{field-1}}\n${\\text{mi}}^{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489236 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "83497943-4dd9-5808-bc36-db659744aaad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489236 #edb/ref 1074 "The exact area of land is ${(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}\\,{\\text{mi}}^{2}.$\n\nWriting ${(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}$ with multiplication signs, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2} & ={{\\frac{4}{5}\\times \\frac{4}{5}}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\times 4}{5\\times 5} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2}=\\frac{16}{25}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489285 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489090 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489285 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166801" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489285 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489285 #edb/ref 1071 "One of the workers cuts $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}\\,\\text{ft}$ from a pipe measuring $5\\,\\frac{1}{8}\\,\\text{ft}.$ What is the length of the remaining pipe? Express your answer as a mixed number.\n\nThe length of the remaining pipe is$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{ft}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489285 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ecc24b66-1c17-5f12-9e7e-a64bd2e2d9c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489285 #edb/ref 1074 "The length of the remaining pipe is $(5\\,\\frac{1}{8}-3\\,\\frac{3}{4})\\text{ft}.$\n\nWriting $5\\,\\frac{1}{8}$ as an improper fraction, we have\n\n$$\n5\\,\\frac{1}{8}=\\frac{5\\times 8+1}{8}=\\frac{41}{8}.\n$$\n\nWriting $3\\,\\frac{3}{4}$ as an improper fraction, we have\n\n$$\n3\\,\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3\\times 4+3}{4}=\\frac{15}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our problem now is to work out the following:\n\n$$\n\\frac{41}{8}-\\frac{15}{4}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with unlike denominators, we need to express each fraction as an equivalent fraction with a common denominator.\n\nIn this question, we can make a common denominator of $8.$\n\nTo put $\\frac{15}{4}$ over a denominator of $8,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{4}=\\frac{15\\times 2}{4\\times 2}=\\frac{30}{8}\n$$\n\nWe can now subtract the fractions. We keep the denominator the same, and we subtract the numerators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{41}{8}-\\frac{30}{8}=\\frac{11}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert back to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{11}{8}=1\\,\\text{R}\\,3=1\\,\\frac{3}{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1\\,\\frac{3}{8}\\,\\text{ft}$ of pipe remains." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489287 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489287 #edb/ref 1069 "q-166800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489287 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489287 #edb/ref 1071 "Of the cement mixture prepared, $1.87$ tons were used to construct the houses. How much cement mixture is left over?\n\nThere are\n{{field-1}}\ntons of cement mixture are left over." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489287 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee99225f-5b1d-5184-84fe-979d439fc52f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489287 #edb/ref 1074 "In part 3, we found that the company prepared $2.29$ tons of cement mixture.\n\nTo determine the amount of cement mixture remaining, we need to calculate $2.29-1.87.$\n\nFirst, we line up the decimal points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we proceed by subtracting the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,\\,\\,\\, &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,7\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,.\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.42$ tons of cement mixture are left over." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489301 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "18e873e5-9337-506c-b540-e1fc8d47545f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489301 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489302 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489310 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489302 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "19f866bd-8dc2-5477-992d-1473853d0c16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489302 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489236 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489303 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489312 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489303 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1f2d7e1e-53f6-5c92-89c3-7c3117f65f5c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489303 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489310 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489354 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489310 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "378f9eb4-6689-57a1-ace0-5895d0bf21e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489310 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489188 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489312 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3e352b3e-ae0c-57b9-9219-0f7ceced29eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489312 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489344 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489344 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9a62d115-e7f9-5bb0-b1b3-7e96b43d7656" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489344 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489354 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186489344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489354 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ae5ab332-2aa1-5052-911b-e0eb68db34fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489354 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186489228 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
